# Repository settings of the pipelines

The workflows in this folder need settings in the GitHub repository.
The generator cannot make these settings.
A repository administrator must make them one time, and again after a change to this file.
{% if infrastructure is not none and (plan or environments) %}

The paths in this file are relative to the folder of the configuration file `dsml.toml`.

## Order of the setup

1. Apply the bootstrap root module of each account in `{{ infrastructure }}/bootstrap/`. The README of each module gives the steps. These modules write the IAM roles that the workflows use.
{% if tooling %}
2. Apply the tooling root module in `{{ infrastructure }}/tooling/` with the credentials of an administrator of the tooling account. This module writes the ECR repositories.
3. Make the GitHub settings in this file.
{% else %}
2. Make the GitHub settings in this file.
{% endif %}

The workflows fail until the IAM roles exist.
{% endif %}
{% if environments %}

## GitHub environments

Make these environments in the settings of the repository.
Use the names exactly as they are in the table.
The trust policy of each deploy role permits only the deploy jobs of its GitHub environment.

| Environment | Workflow | Deployment branches and tags | Required reviewers |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
{% for environment in environments %}
| `{{ environment.name }}` | `{{ environment.workflow }}` | {{ environment.refs | join(", ") }} | {{ "One or more" if environment.reviewed else "None" }} |
{% endfor %}

For each environment, set "Deployment branches and tags" to "Selected branches and tags".
Then add the branches and the tags of the table.
{% for environment in environments if environment.reviewed %}

### Required reviewers of `{{ environment.name }}`

Add one or more required reviewers to the environment `{{ environment.name }}`.
A required reviewer must approve each deployment to `{{ environment.name }}` before the job `deploy-{{ environment.name }}` starts.
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}

## Branch protection of the main branch

Add a branch ruleset for the branch `{{ main_branch }}` with these rules:

1. "Require a pull request before merging".
2. "Require status checks to pass", with these checks. The jobs of `{{ pr_workflow }}` give these checks.
{% for check in checks %}
   - `{{ check }}`
{% endfor %}
3. "Require branches to be up to date before merging".
4. "Block force pushes".
5. "Restrict deletions".

## Repository variables

Add these variables in the settings of the repository, on the tab "Variables" of "Secrets and variables" > "Actions".

| Variable | Value | Workflows |
| --- | --- | --- |
{% for variable in variables %}
| `{{ variable.name }}` | {{ variable.value }} | `{{ variable.workflow }}` |
{% endfor %}

The workflows use no repository secret.
The jobs get AWS credentials only through GitHub OIDC.

## Code scanning

The job `validate` of `{{ pr_workflow }}` sends the findings of the model to GitHub code scanning.
Code scanning must be available for the repository.
For a private repository, GitHub Code Security must be on.
